{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XXb4hX4KM2pKytWrRK4RGU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Classification reformulation提供complexity-dependent scaling advantage：\n2\t  function-level CLS≈CWM null result（三级证据：Qwen3-4B null → 8B diverge 2.43pp → repo-level\n3\t  CWM崩溃）。 DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B复现function-level null result确认结论非Qwen-specific。 Repo-level\n4\t  CLS 3-seed稳定≥85% accuracy，CWM因unparseable≥80%彻底失败。 Complementary errors + oracle\n5\t  ensemble（90.63%）作为bonus contribution。 Diagnostic re-repair以~6pp resolve rate gain验证per-test\n6\t  granularity的实用价值。 Original claims无需调整，三个claim完整成立。Target: EMNLP Main。\n7\t\n8\t  '\n9\timagined_experiments:\n10\t- name: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Construction\n11\t  plan_id: swebench-pertest-data\n12\t  description: 'Docker重新执行SWE-bench Verified patches提取per-test labels。 已通过repo-level实验系列隐式完成（test\n13\t    set 9784 samples, val set 9335 samples）。\n14\t\n15\t    '\n16\t  expected_results:\n17\t    n_instances_target: 500\n18\t    n_instances_successful: 489\n19\t    n_instances_docker_fail: 11\n20\t    total_test_samples: 9784\n21\t    total_val_samples: 9335\n22\t    avg_f2p_tests_per_instance: 3.0\n23\t    median_f2p_tests: 2\n24\t    avg_p2p_tests_per_instance: 47.8\n25\t    f2p_T1_pct: 68.7\n26\t    f2p_T2_pct: 19.1\n27\t    f2p_T3plus_pct: 12.2\n28\t    docker_wall_clock_hours: 18.5\n29\t    n_parallel_containers: 16\n30\t    label_agreement_with_original_pct: 98.7\n31\t    flaky_test_rate_pct: 1.0\n32\t    class_balance_pass_pct: 72.96\n33\t    class_balance_fail_pct: 27.04\n34\t  result_rationale: '489/500成功率（97.8%）略高于前次预测，因为SWE-bench Verified本身经过质量筛选， Docker环境兼容性好于完整SWE-bench。11个失败主要来自极老repo的Python\n35\t    3.7依赖 和少量C extension编译失败。F2P分布与SWE-bench Verified已知统计一致（median=2, mean=3）。 类别不平衡72.96%\n36\t    pass / 27.04% fail与repo-level-cls-v5实验的majority baseline吻合。 98.7% label agreement验证Docker\n37\t    re-evaluation的方法论可靠性—— 1.3%不一致来自flaky tests（1.0%）和时间敏感assertions（0.3%）。 数据集本身是独立resource\n38\t    contribution，使任何future work on SWE-bench per-test verification成为可能。\n39\t\n40\t    '\n41\t  tables:\n42\t  - name: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\n43\t    columns:\n44\t    - Statistic\n45\t    - Value\n46\t    rows:\n47\t    - - Instances (successful)\n48\t      - 489\n49\t    - - Candidates per instance\n50\t      - 16\n51\t    - - Total test-level samples\n52\t      - 9784\n53\t    - - Avg F2P tests/instance\n54\t      - 3.0\n55\t    - - Median F2P tests\n56\t      - 2\n57\t    - - Avg P2P tests/instance\n58\t      - 47.8\n59\t    - - Class balance (pass%)\n60\t      - 72.96%\n61\t    - - Label agreement\n62\t      - 98.7%\n63\t  figures_description:\n64\t  - F2P test count histogram (T=1 to T=10+)，展示T=1占68.7%的长尾分布\n65\t  - Per-instance total test count distribution，展示repo-level测试规模\n66\t  analysis: '数据集已通过repo-level实验系列隐式构建并验证。F2P分布确认31.3%的instances有T≥2， 为per-test advantage提供足够的multi-F2P样本。P2P测试数量大（avg\n67\t    47.8）但regression rate ~1% 意味着P2P对per-test advantage贡献极小。数据集的主要价值是enable repo-level\n68\t    CLS vs CWM对比。\n69\t\n70\t    '\n71\t- name: Repo-Level CLS Multi-Seed Validation (8B)\n72\t  plan_id: repo-level-training\n73\t  description: 'Qwen3-8B LoRA classification在repo-level SWE-bench-PerTest上的3-seed验证。\n74\t    当前有s42 (ckpt400, 84.79%)和seed123 (ckpt3000, 85.6%)，需第3个seed并统一checkpoint selection策略。\n75\t    Best tier要求mean accuracy≥85%, fail_f1≥75%。\n76\t\n77\t    '\n78\t  expected_results:\n79\t    seed42_accuracy: 84.79\n80\t    seed42_fail_f1: 72.93\n81\t    seed42_pass_f1: 89.43\n82\t    seed42_checkpoint: ckpt-400\n83\t    seed123_accuracy: 85.8\n84\t    seed123_fail_f1: 76.2\n85\t    seed123_pass_f1: 90.1\n86\t    seed123_checkpoint: ckpt-500\n87\t    seed456_accuracy: 85.9\n88\t    seed456_fail_f1: 76.8\n89\t    seed456_pass_f1: 90.5\n90\t    seed456_checkpoint: ckpt-450\n91\t    mean_accuracy: 85.5\n92\t    std_accuracy: 0.61\n93\t    mean_fail_f1: 75.3\n94\t    std_fail_f1: 2.1\n95\t    mean_pass_f1: 90.0\n96\t    mean_f1_macro: 82.7\n97\t    unparseable_all_seeds: 0\n98\t    bootstrap_ci_accuracy_95:\n99\t    - 84.6\n100\t    - 86.4\n101\t  result_rationale: '当前s42 ckpt400的72.93% fail_f1是所有8B repo-level实验中最高的—— 原因是ckpt400处于early-stopping\n102\t    sweet spot，fail precision(70.32%)和recall(75.74%)相对平衡。 seed123的ckpt3000训练过长导致严重的precision-recall偏移：precision_fail高达91.65%但recall_fail仅51.44%，\n103\t    模型过度保守地预测fail（宁可漏报不误报），导致fail_f1=65.89%。 Best tier假设统一checkpoint selection策略（按val\n104\t    fail_f1选最佳ckpt而非按accuracy）， seed123在ckpt500附近可以恢复fail recall到~68%，将fail_f1提升至76.2%。\n105\t    seed456作为新seed，在相同selection策略下预期表现与seed123相近。 3-seed mean accuracy 85.5%稳定在[84,88]范围中部，std=0.61pp反映正常的LoRA初始化随机性。\n106\t    fail_f1 mean 75.3%在[72,82]范围下部但≥75%，验证CLS在repo-level的稳定性。 关键洞察：repo-level CLS从function-level\n107\t    88.41%下降到85.5%（-2.9pp）， 下降幅度远小于CWM（从87.4%崩溃到<55%）——这是complexity-dependent advantage的核心证据。\n108\t\n109\t    '\n110\t  tables:\n111\t  - name: Repo-Level CLS 8B Multi-Seed Results\n112\t    columns:\n113\t    - Seed\n114\t    - Checkpoint\n115\t    - Accuracy\n116\t    - Fail F1\n117\t    - Pass F1\n118\t    - F1 Macro\n119\t    rows:\n120\t    - - 42\n121\t      - ckpt-400\n122\t      - 84.79%\n123\t      - 72.93%\n124\t      - 89.43%\n125\t      - 81.18%\n126\t    - - 123\n127\t      - ckpt-500\n128\t      - 85.8%\n129\t      - 76.2%\n130\t      - 90.1%\n131\t      - 83.2%\n132\t    - - 456\n133\t      - ckpt-450\n134\t      - 85.9%\n135\t      - 76.8%\n136\t      - 90.5%\n137\t      - 83.7%\n138\t    - - Mean±Std\n139\t      - —\n140\t      - 85.5±0.61\n141\t      - 75.3±2.1\n142\t      - 90.0±0.5\n143\t      - 82.7±1.3\n144\t  - name: Function-Level → Repo-Level Drop (CLS vs CWM)\n145\t    columns:\n146\t    - Level\n147\t    - CLS Accuracy (3-seed)\n148\t    - CWM Accuracy\n149\t    - Gap (pp)\n150\t    rows:\n151\t    - - Function (4B)\n152\t      - 88.41%\n153\t      - 87.4%\n154\t      - '+1.0'\n155\t    - - Function (8B)\n156\t      - 89.75%\n157\t      - 87.3%\n158\t      - '+2.43'\n159\t    - - Repo (8B)\n160\t      - 85.5%\n161\t      - <55%*\n162\t      - '>30'\n163\t    footnotes:\n164\t    - '*CWM repo accuracy estimated from parseable predictions only; overall accuracy\n165\t      <55% due to ≥85% unparseable rate'\n166\t  figures_description:\n167\t  - 3-seed accuracy + fail_f1 box plot with CI，展示跨seed稳定性\n168\t  - Function-to-Repo drop comparison bar chart：CLS -2.9pp vs CWM -32+pp\n169\t  analysis: 'Multi-seed验证是best tier的核心数据基础。3-seed std=0.61pp证明repo-level CLS结果不是单次实验的偶然。\n170\t    与function-level的std=0.96pp相比，repo-level variance更小， 可能因为repo-level数据集更大（9784 vs\n171\t    1890 samples），averaging效应更强。 fail_f1的std=2.1pp较大，反映checkpoint selection对precision-recall\n172\t    tradeoff敏感—— 但mean 75.3%稳定≥75%，证明CLS可以在repo-level可靠地检测failing tests。\n173\t\n174\t    '\n175\t- name: Repo-Level CWM Unparseable Rate Confirmation\n176\t  plan_id: repo-level-training\n177\t  description: '确认CWM在repo-level的unparseable rate≥80%是formulation固有缺陷。 整合现有cwm-v10(93%),\n178\t    v11(75.2%), v12(53.7%), cwm-seed123-conda(67.2%)的数据。 用标准化generation config（max_new_tokens=512,\n179\t    匹配典型test output长度）重新评估。\n180\t\n181\t    '\n182\t  expected_results:\n183\t    cwm_8b_unparseable_rate: 0.85\n184\t    cwm_8b_accuracy_overall: 0.52\n185\t    cwm_8b_accuracy_parseable_only: 0.64\n186\t    cwm_8b_fail_f1: 0.18\n187\t    cwm_8b_pass_f1: 0.67\n188\t    cwm_8b_f1_macro: 0.42\n189\t    cwm_8b_truncated_pct: 0.38\n190\t    cwm_8b_string_mismatch_pct: 0.22\n191\t    cwm_8b_clean_correct_pct: 0.1\n192\t    cwm_4b_unparseable_rate: 0.88\n193\t    cwm_4b_accuracy_overall: 0.48\n194\t    majority_baseline: 0.7296\n195\t    cwm_vs_majority_gap_pp: -21.0\n196\t    generation_length_mean_tokens: 487\n197\t    generation_length_median_tokens: 512\n198\t  result_rationale: '现有数据已强烈支持unparseable≥80%：cwm-v10在max_new_tokens=64时93%， cwm-v11在1024时75.2%（但该实验用了subset500且可能有config差异）。\n199\t    标准化config（max_new_tokens=512）下预期85%，原因： (1) Repo-level test execution output通常包含完整stack\n200\t    trace（200-2000 tokens）、 文件路径、版本号、格式化数据结构——CWM需要精确复现这些才能推导pass/fail， 但4B/8B模型无法忠实生成如此复杂的结构化文本；\n201\t    (2) 即使生成了看似合理的output，string-level exact match极低（v10: exact_match约10%）， 因为一个字符的差异（路径分隔符、空格、换行）就导致mismatch；\n202\t    (3) Token budget exhaustion在512 tokens时仍影响38%的predictions—— 许多test output超过512\n203\t    tokens，truncation导致判断信息丢失。 关键论点：CWM的85% unparseable不是调参不足（已尝试10+版本，不同rank/alpha/generation\n204\t    length）， 而是generation formulation在repo-level complexity下的结构性失败—— 要求模型精确生成数百token的结构化文本是一个远难于binary\n205\t    classification的任务。 Overall accuracy 52%低于majority baseline（72.96%），证明CWM在repo-level不仅无优势，\n206\t    实际上worse than trivial baseline。\n207\t\n208\t    '\n209\t  tables:\n210\t  - name: Repo-Level CWM Failure Mode Breakdown\n211\t    columns:\n212\t    - Category\n213\t    - '% of Predictions'\n214\t    - Description\n215\t    rows:\n216\t    - - Unparseable (total)\n217\t      - 85%\n218\t      - Cannot extract pass/fail from generation\n219\t    - - — Token exhaustion\n220\t      - 38%\n221\t      - Output truncated at max_new_tokens\n222\t    - - — Format failure\n223\t      - 28%\n224\t      - Output structurally invalid\n225\t    - - — String mismatch\n226\t      - 19%\n227\t      - Parseable but wrong surface form\n228\t    - - Parseable & correct\n229\t      - 10%\n230\t      - CWM produces correct output\n231\t    - - Parseable & wrong\n232\t      - 5%\n233\t      - Clean but incorrect prediction\n234\t  - name: CWM Evolution Across Versions\n235\t    columns:\n236\t    - Version\n237\t    - max_new_tokens\n238\t    - Unparseable%\n239\t    - Accuracy%\n240\t    rows:\n241\t    - - v10\n242\t      - 64\n243\t      - 93%\n244\t      - 69.9%*\n245\t    - - v11\n246\t      - 1024\n247\t      - 75.2%\n248\t      - 66.6%\n249\t    - - v12\n250\t      - 512\n251\t      - 53.7%**\n252\t      - 58.0%\n253\t    - - seed123-conda\n254\t      - 512\n255\t      - 67.2%\n256\t      - 59.1%\n257\t    - - Best-tier (standardized)\n258\t      - 512\n259\t      - 85%\n260\t      - 52%\n261\t    footnotes:\n262\t    - '*v10 accuracy inflated: unparseable treated as majority-class prediction'\n263\t    - '**v12 used different training config (longer training, lower LR)'\n264\t  figures_description:\n265\t  - Unparseable rate vs max_new_tokens curve，展示generation length与parsability的tradeoff\n266\t  - CWM failure mode stacked bar：token exhaustion + format failure + string mismatch\n267\t    = 85% total\n268\t  analysis: 'CWM的repo-level失败是formulation-level的必然结果，不是工程问题。 10+版本的迭代（v1到v12，不同seed，不同LoRA配置）consistently产生50-93%\n269\t    unparseable rate， 说明问题出在task formulation而非model/training细节。 这为Claim 1提供了最强的对比：CLS在相同数据上85.5%\n270\t    accuracy vs CWM 52%—— gap超过30pp，远超function-level的0-2.43pp。 Complexity-dependent\n271\t    advantage的narrative完整成立。\n272\t\n273\t    '\n274\t- name: DeepSeek Function-Level Classification\n275\t  plan_id: deepseek-cls-func\n276\t  description: 'DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B-Instruct LoRA fine-tune做function-level per-test\n277\t    binary classification。 与Qwen3-4B CLS对比，验证CLS formulation advantage不是Qwen-specific。\n278\t\n279\t    '\n280\t  expected_results:\n281\t    accuracy: 86.3\n282\t    pass_f1: 86.0\n283\t    fail_f1: 86.5\n284\t    f1_macro: 86.3\n285\t    pass_precision: 90.8\n286\t    pass_recall: 81.5\n287\t    fail_precision: 82.2\n288\t    fail_recall: 91.2\n289\t    train_loss: 0.265\n290\t    eval_loss: 0.078\n291\t    unparseable: 0\n292\t    test_set_size: 1890\n293\t  result_rationale: 'DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B（2023年12月）比Qwen3-4B（2025年5月）多~1.7x参数， 但属于旧generation，code\n294\t    understanding能力与Qwen3-4B大致equivalent。 预期accuracy 86.3%略低于Qwen3-4B multi-seed mean（88.41%），\n295\t    因为DeepSeek的pretraining data cutoff更早，对newer coding patterns覆盖不足。 但86.3%仍然远高于majority\n296\t    baseline（51.75%）和zero-shot LLM-judge（64.4%）， 证明fine-tuned classification在不同架构上consistently有效。\n297\t    关键发现：DeepSeek CLS accuracy（86.3%）与DeepSeek CWM accuracy（85.7%）的gap仅0.6pp—— 这复现了Qwen3-4B上的null\n298\t    result（gap 1.0pp at 4B）， 确认function-level CLS≈CWM equivalence是architecture-independent的。\n299\t\n300\t    '\n301\t  tables: []\n302\t  figures_description: []\n303\t  analysis: 'DeepSeek CLS结果是hypothesis 3的关键支撑。 如果gap仅在Qwen上存在，reviewer可以质疑这是Qwen-specific\n304\t    artifact。 DeepSeek复现消除了这个concern。\n305\t\n306\t    '\n307\t- name: DeepSeek Function-Level CWM + Multi-Seed\n308\t  plan_id: deepseek-cwm-func\n309\t  description: 'DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B LoRA CWM generation baseline + seed123多seed验证。\n310\t    与DeepSeek CLS对比确认function-level null result的architecture independence。\n311\t\n312\t    '\n313\t  expected_results:\n314\t    seed42_cwm_accuracy: 85.7\n315\t    seed42_cwm_pass_f1: 85.4\n316\t    seed42_cwm_fail_f1: 86.0\n317\t    seed42_cwm_exact_match: 80.5\n318\t    seed42_cwm_unparseable: 0\n319\t    seed123_cwm_accuracy: 86.1\n320\t    seed123_cwm_pass_f1: 85.8\n321\t    seed123_cwm_fail_f1: 86.3\n322\t    seed42_cls_accuracy: 86.3\n323\t    cls_cwm_gap_seed42_pp: 0.6\n324\t    cls_cwm_gap_seed123_pp: 0.2\n325\t    cls_cwm_gap_mean_pp: 0.4\n326\t    cls_cwm_gap_95ci_lower: -0.9\n327\t    cls_cwm_gap_95ci_upper: 1.7\n328\t    paired_ttest_pvalue: 0.68\n329\t  result_rationale: 'DeepSeek CWM在function-level预期accuracy 85.7%，与CLS的86.3%差距仅0.6pp。\n330\t    这复现了Qwen3-4B上的pattern：CWM 87.4% vs CLS 88.41%（gap ~1.0pp）。 DeepSeek的exact match\n331\t    rate（80.5%）低于Qwen3-4B（84.02%）， 因为DeepSeek对function-level output format的生成精度略低——\n332\t    但由于function-level output短（<50 tokens），这些format差异不影响pass/fail判断。 seed123 CWM（86.1%）与seed42（85.7%）的差异（0.4pp）在正常随机性范围内。\n333\t    两seed的CLS-CWM gap（0.6pp和0.2pp）mean=0.4pp，95% CI [-0.9, 1.7]包含0， p=0.68远超0.05，cleanly确认function-level\n334\t    null result。 关键指标：deepseek_func_cls_cwm_gap_pp = 0.4pp，在best tier范围[-1.0, 1.5]内。\n335\t\n336\t    '\n337\t  tables:\n338\t  - name: DeepSeek vs Qwen Function-Level Comparison\n339\t    columns:\n340\t    - Architecture\n341\t    - Size\n342\t    - CLS Acc\n343\t    - CWM Acc\n344\t    - Gap (pp)\n345\t    rows:\n346\t    - - Qwen3\n347\t      - 4B\n348\t      - 88.41%\n349\t      - 87.4%\n350\t      - '+1.0'\n351\t    - - Qwen3\n352\t      - 8B\n353\t      - 89.75%\n354\t      - 87.3%\n355\t      - '+2.43'\n356\t    - - DeepSeek-Coder\n357\t      - 6.7B\n358\t      - 86.3%\n359\t      - 85.7%\n360\t      - '+0.6'\n361\t  - name: DeepSeek Multi-Seed CWM\n362\t    columns:\n363\t    - Seed\n364\t    - CWM Acc\n365\t    - CLS Acc\n366\t    - Gap (pp)\n367\t    rows:\n368\t    - - 42\n369\t      - 85.7%\n370\t      - 86.3%\n371\t      - '+0.6'\n372\t    - - 123\n373\t      - 86.1%\n374\t      - 86.3%*\n375\t      - '+0.2'\n376\t    - - Mean\n377\t      - 85.9%\n378\t      - 86.3%\n379\t      - '+0.4'\n380\t    footnotes:\n381\t    - '*CLS只训练了seed42，此处复用同一CLS模型'\n382\t  figures_description:\n383\t  - Architecture-independent null result visualization：Qwen3-4B, Qwen3-8B, DeepSeek-6.7B三组bar\n384\t    pairs，function-level gap均在噪声范围内\n385\t  - DeepSeek CLS vs CWM per-class F1 comparison，CI完全重叠\n386\t  analysis: 'DeepSeek复现是best tier叙事的关键一环。三个architecture×size配置的function-level gap：\n387\t    Qwen3-4B: +1.0pp, Qwen3-8B: +2.43pp, DeepSeek-6.7B: +0.6pp。 function-level gap始终在0-2.5pp范围内，与repo-level\n388\t    >30pp形成鲜明对比。 这排除了\"CLS advantage是Qwen architecture artifact\"的reviewer concern。\n389\t    注意Qwen3-8B的2.43pp gap已经开始diverge——这preview了repo-level的趋势， 更大模型+更复杂任务下CWM failure\n390\t    modes逐渐显现。 DeepSeek作为完全不同的architecture（不同tokenizer、不同attention实现、不同pretraining\n391\t    data） 仍然reproduce null result，说明这是task-level property而非model-level artifact。\n392\t\n393\t    '\n394\t- name: DeepSeek Repo-Level Classification\n395\t  plan_id: deepseek-cls-repo\n396\t  description: 'DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B LoRA classification在repo-level SWE-bench-PerTest数据上。\n397\t    验证classification formulation的repo-level advantage在不同architecture下是否保持。\n398\t\n399\t    '\n400\t  expected_results:\n401\t    accuracy: 81.5\n402\t    f1_macro: 76.8\n403\t    fail_f1: 65.2\n404\t    pass_f1: 88.4\n405\t    fail_precision: 68.5\n406\t    fail_recall: 62.1\n407\t    pass_precision: 85.3\n408\t    pass_recall: 91.7\n409\t    unparseable: 0\n410\t    majority_baseline: 72.96\n411\t    gap_vs_majority_pp: 8.5\n412\t    qwen8b_repo_accuracy: 85.5\n413\t    deepseek_vs_qwen_gap_pp: -4.0\n414\t    deepseek_func_to_repo_drop_pp: -4.8\n415\t  result_rationale: 'DeepSeek repo-level CLS预期81.5% accuracy，低于Qwen3-8B的85.5%（-4.0pp），原因：\n416\t    (1) DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B的context window限制（16K vs Qwen3-8B的32K）， repo-level input平均6.8K\n417\t    tokens，更多cases需要truncation； (2) DeepSeek的code understanding在repo-level cross-file\n418\t    dependencies上弱于newer Qwen3， pretraining data中repo-level code comprehension的覆盖不足；\n419\t    (3) 6.7B vs 8B的参数差距虽小，但Qwen3架构效率更高（GQA + sliding window attention）。 从function-level\n420\t    86.3%到repo-level 81.5%的drop（-4.8pp）与Qwen3-8B的drop（-4.3pp）相近， 说明classification\n421\t    formulation在不同architecture上有consistent的degradation pattern。 关键发现：DeepSeek repo-level\n422\t    CLS（81.5%）仍然远高于majority baseline（72.96%）， 证明classification formulation即使在非SOTA\n423\t    architecture上也能provide reliable verification。 如果DeepSeek CWM repo-level也像Qwen\n424\t    CWM一样unparseable≥80%， 则完全确认advantage是formulation-driven而非architecture-driven。\n425\t\n426\t    '\n427\t  tables:\n428\t  - name: Cross-Architecture Repo-Level CLS Comparison\n429\t    columns:\n430\t    - Architecture\n431\t    - Size\n432\t    - Func CLS Acc\n433\t    - Repo CLS Acc\n434\t    - Drop (pp)\n435\t    rows:\n436\t    - - Qwen3\n437\t      - 4B\n438\t      - 88.41%\n439\t      - ~83.6%*\n440\t      - -4.8\n441\t    - - Qwen3\n442\t      - 8B\n443\t      - 89.75%\n444\t      - 85.5%\n445\t      - -4.3\n446\t    - - DeepSeek-Coder\n447\t      - 6.7B\n448\t      - 86.3%\n449\t      - 81.5%\n450\t      - -4.8\n451\t    footnotes:\n452\t    - '*4B repo results from cls4b-v5-ckpt4600 test eval'\n453\t  figures_description:\n454\t  - Function → Repo accuracy drop comparison across architectures，三组paired bars展示consistent\n455\t    ~4-5pp drop\n456\t  analysis: 'DeepSeek repo-level CLS是supplementary evidence，不是核心result。 其价值在于展示classification\n457\t    formulation的robustness across architectures： 即使换一个完全不同的model family，repo-level\n458\t    CLS仍然work（>>majority baseline）， 而CWM仍然fail（unparseable dominant）。 这是architecture\n459\t    independence claim在repo-level的延伸验证。\n460\t\n461\t    '\n462\t- name: Repo-Level Error Complementarity & Oracle Ensemble\n463\t  plan_id: repo-level-training\n464\t  description: '分析repo-level CLS和CWM（parseable subset）的error complementarity。 计算oracle\n465\t    ensemble accuracy——如果两个模型的错误不重叠，ensemble ceiling多高。 扩展function-level的complementarity\n466\t    finding（oracle=90.63%）到repo-level。\n467\t\n468\t    '\n469\t  expected_results:\n470\t    cls_repo_accuracy: 85.5\n471\t    cwm_repo_accuracy_parseable: 64.0\n472\t    cwm_repo_parseable_pct: 15.0\n473\t    oracle_accuracy_parseable_subset: 91.2\n474\t    cls_error_type_dominant: miss_bug (false_negative)\n475\t    cwm_error_type_dominant: false_alarm + unparseable\n476\t    complementarity_rate: 0.68\n477\t    cls_only_correct_pct: 34.5\n478\t    cwm_only_correct_pct: 8.2\n479\t    both_correct_pct: 48.8\n480\t    both_wrong_pct: 8.5\n481\t    n_parseable_samples: 1468\n482\t  result_rationale: 'Repo-level complementarity analysis限于CWM parseable subset（~15%\n483\t    of total，~1468 samples）。 在这个subset上，CLS accuracy ~85.5%，CWM accuracy ~64%—— 但两者的error\n484\t    pattern高度complementary（complementarity rate 0.68）。 CLS的dominant error是miss bugs（false\n485\t    negative）：模型对长context中的subtle bugs不敏感， 倾向于predict pass。CWM的dominant error是false\n486\t    alarms： 生成的output与gold不完全match被判为fail，即使语义上patch是correct的。 Oracle ensemble在parseable\n487\t    subset上达91.2%，证明两种formulation捕获不同的code semantics。 但CWM的85% unparseable严重限制了ensemble的实际应用——\n488\t    只有15%的predictions可以ensemble，对overall accuracy的提升有限。 这为paper提供了nuanced finding：complementarity存在但CWM的formulation\n489\t    bottleneck 使其无法被充分利用。Future work可以探索更好的generation formulation来保留complementarity\n490\t    同时降低unparseable rate。\n491\t\n492\t    '\n493\t  tables:\n494\t  - name: Repo-Level Error Complementarity (Parseable Subset)\n495\t    columns:\n496\t    - Category\n497\t    - '%'\n498\t    rows:\n499\t    - - Both correct\n500\t      - 48.8%\n501\t    - - CLS only correct\n502\t      - 34.5%\n503\t    - - CWM only correct\n504\t      - 8.2%\n505\t    - - Both wrong\n506\t      - 8.5%\n507\t    - - Oracle accuracy\n508\t      - 91.2%\n509\t  - name: Function vs Repo Error Complementarity\n510\t    columns:\n511\t    - Level\n512\t    - CLS Acc\n513\t    - CWM Acc\n514\t    - Oracle Acc\n515\t    - Complementarity\n516\t    rows:\n517\t    - - Function (4B)\n518\t      - 87.5%\n519\t      - 87.5%\n520\t      - 90.63%\n521\t      - 0.72\n522\t    - - Repo (8B, parseable)\n523\t      - 85.5%\n524\t      - 64.0%\n525\t      - 91.2%\n526\t      - 0.68\n527\t  figures_description:\n528\t  - Venn diagram of error overlap at repo-level，展示CLS和CWM的error union structure\n529\t  analysis: 'Repo-level complementarity结果有两面性： (1) 好消息：在parseable subset上oracle达91.2%，与function-level的90.63%相近，\n530\t    说明CLS和CWM在能work的cases上仍然是complementary的。 (2) 坏消息：85% unparseable意味着ensemble只覆盖15%的predictions。\n531\t    论文中应frame为：complementarity是formulation-level property（与complexity无关）， 但CWM的generation\n532\t    bottleneck在高complexity下限制了其utility。 这motivates future work on improved generation\n533\t    formulations that maintain complementarity while achieving better parsability。\n534\t\n535\t    '\n536\t- name: Diagnostic Re-repair Experiment\n537\t  plan_id: diagnostic-rerepair\n538\t  description: '200-instance downstream proof-of-concept：repair agent在per-test failure\n539\t    predictions 指导下vs无per-test信息，比较resolve rate。使用SWE-agent framework。\n540\t\n541\t    '\n542\t  expected_results:\n543\t    n_instances: 200\n544\t    baseline_resolve_rate_pct: 27.0\n545\t    rerepair_blind_resolve_rate_pct: 29.5\n546\t    rerepair_with_diagnostics_resolve_rate_pct: 33.0\n547\t    diagnostic_lift_pp: 6.0\n548\t    blind_lift_pp: 2.5\n549\t    diagnostic_specific_lift_pp: 3.5\n550\t    n_initially_unresolved: 146\n551\t    n_rerepair_triggered: 92\n552\t    rerepair_success_with_diag_pct: 25.0\n553\t    rerepair_success_without_diag_pct: 13.0\n554\t    mcnemar_pvalue: 0.022\n555\t    multi_f2p_diagnostic_lift_pp: 11.5\n556\t    single_f2p_diagnostic_lift_pp: 2.0\n557\t    multi_f2p_n_instances: 62\n558\t    single_f2p_n_instances: 138\n559\t    avg_rerepair_attempts: 1.8\n560\t    per_test_prediction_accuracy_on_tested: 84.2\n561\t  result_rationale: 'Diagnostic lift 6.0pp（best tier范围[3,8]）的机制： (1) Per-test predictions为repair\n562\t    agent提供failure localization—— 当agent知道\"test_parse_edge_case fails but test_basic\n563\t    passes\"时， 修复集中在edge case logic而非盲目重试entire solution； (2) Blind re-repair（知道unresolved但不知哪个test\n564\t    fail）仍有2.5pp lift， 因为SWE-agent的retry本身就有correction概率—— 但diagnostic-specific增量3.5pp证明per-test信息的独特贡献；\n565\t    (3) 优势严重集中于multi-F2P instances： T≥2时lift 11.5pp vs T=1时仅2.0pp，与oracle analysis预测完全一致。\n566\t    原因：T=1时per-test info等价于trajectory info（只有一个fail test， 知道\"有test fail\"和知道\"test_X\n567\t    fail\"信息量相同）； T≥2时per-test info区分了不同failure patterns， repair agent可以逐个target failing\n568\t    tests而非guess which test fails。 McNemar p=0.022在200样本下达到显著性（<0.05）—— 虽然样本量有限但足以支撑proof-of-concept级别的claim。\n569\t    92/146 re-repair triggered表明63%的unresolved instances至少尝试了re-repair； with diagnostics的25%\n570\t    success rate vs without的13%证明信息质量差异。 Per-test prediction accuracy on re-repair测试的84.2%与overall\n571\t    85.5%接近， 说明re-repair并未选择性地作用于easy/hard cases。\n572\t\n573\t    '\n574\t  tables:\n575\t  - name: Diagnostic Re-repair Results\n576\t    columns:\n577\t    - Condition\n578\t    - Resolve Rate\n579\t    - Δ vs Baseline\n580\t    rows:\n581\t    - - No re-repair (baseline)\n582\t      - 27.0%\n583\t      - —\n584\t    - - Re-repair without diagnostics\n585\t      - 29.5%\n586\t      - +2.5 pp\n587\t    - - Re-repair with per-test diagnostics\n588\t      - 33.0%\n589\t      - +6.0 pp\n590\t    - - Diagnostic-specific lift\n591\t      - —\n592\t      - +3.5 pp (p=0.022)\n593\t  - name: Diagnostic Lift Stratified by F2P Count\n594\t    columns:\n595\t    - F2P Count\n596\t    - N Instances\n597\t    - Diag Lift\n598\t    - Blind Lift\n599\t    rows:\n600\t    - - T=1\n601\t      - 138\n602\t      - +2.0 pp\n603\t      - +1.5 pp\n604\t    - - T≥2\n605\t      - 62\n606\t      - +11.5 pp\n607\t      - +3.8 pp\n608\t    - - Overall\n609\t      - 200\n610\t      - +6.0 pp\n611\t      - +2.5 pp\n612\t  figures_description:\n613\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: three conditions × T=1 vs T≥2 stratification'\n614\t  - 'Per-instance resolve rate improvement scatter: x=N failing tests, y=resolve rate\n615\t    delta'\n616\t  analysis: Re-repair实验完成了Claim 2的实证闭环：per-test classification不仅在accuracy上等价于trajectory\n617\t    （TOST p=0.007），还提供了actionable的diagnostic信息带来6pp resolve rate improvement。 Stratification连接Claim\n618\t    2和Claim 3：advantage集中在multi-F2P instances（与oracle预测一致）， 为部署决策提供了清晰框架——在multi-F2P场景下per-test\n619\t    verification的ROI最高。 论文应定位为proof-of-concept，目标是展示mechanism而非claim SOTA repair performance。\n620\t    200 instances是moderate sample size，sufficient for significance但reviewer可能要求larger\n621\t    scale—— frame为future work方向。\n622\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb1cd3bd-4c39-4492-be2f-2de9468a472a","uuid":"1240be68-9bb9-4684-94da-4a09fa6a2b2f","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:17:40.372Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T073712/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Classification reformulation提供complexity-dependent scaling advantage：\n  function-level CLS≈CWM null result（三级证据：Qwen3-4B null → 8B diverge 2.43pp → repo-level\n  CWM崩溃）。 DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B复现function-level null result确认结论非Qwen-specific。 Repo-level\n  CLS 3-seed稳定≥85% accuracy，CWM因unparseable≥80%彻底失败。 Complementary errors + oracle\n  ensemble（90.63%）作为bonus contribution。 Diagnostic re-repair以~6pp resolve rate gain验证per-test\n  granularity的实用价值。 Original claims无需调整，三个claim完整成立。Target: EMNLP Main。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Construction\n  plan_id: swebench-pertest-data\n  description: 'Docker重新执行SWE-bench Verified patches提取per-test labels。 已通过repo-level实验系列隐式完成（test\n    set 9784 samples, val set 9335 samples）。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_instances_target: 500\n    n_instances_successful: 489\n    n_instances_docker_fail: 11\n    total_test_samples: 9784\n    total_val_samples: 9335\n    avg_f2p_tests_per_instance: 3.0\n    median_f2p_tests: 2\n    avg_p2p_tests_per_instance: 47.8\n    f2p_T1_pct: 68.7\n    f2p_T2_pct: 19.1\n    f2p_T3plus_pct: 12.2\n    docker_wall_clock_hours: 18.5\n    n_parallel_containers: 16\n    label_agreement_with_original_pct: 98.7\n    flaky_test_rate_pct: 1.0\n    class_balance_pass_pct: 72.96\n    class_balance_fail_pct: 27.04\n  result_rationale: '489/500成功率（97.8%）略高于前次预测，因为SWE-bench Verified本身经过质量筛选， Docker环境兼容性好于完整SWE-bench。11个失败主要来自极老repo的Python\n    3.7依赖 和少量C extension编译失败。F2P分布与SWE-bench Verified已知统计一致（median=2, mean=3）。 类别不平衡72.96%\n    pass / 27.04% fail与repo-level-cls-v5实验的majority baseline吻合。 98.7% label agreement验证Docker\n    re-evaluation的方法论可靠性—— 1.3%不一致来自flaky tests（1.0%）和时间敏感assertions（0.3%）。 数据集本身是独立resource\n    contribution，使任何future work on SWE-bench per-test verification成为可能。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\n    columns:\n    - Statistic\n    - Value\n    rows:\n    - - Instances (successful)\n      - 489\n    - - Candidates per instance\n      - 16\n    - - Total test-level samples\n      - 9784\n    - - Avg F2P tests/instance\n      - 3.0\n    - - Median F2P tests\n      - 2\n    - - Avg P2P tests/instance\n      - 47.8\n    - - Class balance (pass%)\n      - 72.96%\n    - - Label agreement\n      - 98.7%\n  figures_description:\n  - F2P test count histogram (T=1 to T=10+)，展示T=1占68.7%的长尾分布\n  - Per-instance total test count distribution，展示repo-level测试规模\n  analysis: '数据集已通过repo-level实验系列隐式构建并验证。F2P分布确认31.3%的instances有T≥2， 为per-test advantage提供足够的multi-F2P样本。P2P测试数量大（avg\n    47.8）但regression rate ~1% 意味着P2P对per-test advantage贡献极小。数据集的主要价值是enable repo-level\n    CLS vs CWM对比。\n\n    '\n- name: Repo-Level CLS Multi-Seed Validation (8B)\n  plan_id: repo-level-training\n  description: 'Qwen3-8B LoRA classification在repo-level SWE-bench-PerTest上的3-seed验证。\n    当前有s42 (ckpt400, 84.79%)和seed123 (ckpt3000, 85.6%)，需第3个seed并统一checkpoint selection策略。\n    Best tier要求mean accuracy≥85%, fail_f1≥75%。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    seed42_accuracy: 84.79\n    seed42_fail_f1: 72.93\n    seed42_pass_f1: 89.43\n    seed42_checkpoint: ckpt-400\n    seed123_accuracy: 85.8\n    seed123_fail_f1: 76.2\n    seed123_pass_f1: 90.1\n    seed123_checkpoint: ckpt-500\n    seed456_accuracy: 85.9\n    seed456_fail_f1: 76.8\n    seed456_pass_f1: 90.5\n    seed456_checkpoint: ckpt-450\n    mean_accuracy: 85.5\n    std_accuracy: 0.61\n    mean_fail_f1: 75.3\n    std_fail_f1: 2.1\n    mean_pass_f1: 90.0\n    mean_f1_macro: 82.7\n    unparseable_all_seeds: 0\n    bootstrap_ci_accuracy_95:\n    - 84.6\n    - 86.4\n  result_rationale: '当前s42 ckpt400的72.93% fail_f1是所有8B repo-level实验中最高的—— 原因是ckpt400处于early-stopping\n    sweet spot，fail precision(70.32%)和recall(75.74%)相对平衡。 seed123的ckpt3000训练过长导致严重的precision-recall偏移：precision_fail高达91.65%但recall_fail仅51.44%，\n    模型过度保守地预测fail（宁可漏报不误报），导致fail_f1=65.89%。 Best tier假设统一checkpoint selection策略（按val\n    fail_f1选最佳ckpt而非按accuracy）， seed123在ckpt500附近可以恢复fail recall到~68%，将fail_f1提升至76.2%。\n    seed456作为新seed，在相同selection策略下预期表现与seed123相近。 3-seed mean accuracy 85.5%稳定在[84,88]范围中部，std=0.61pp反映正常的LoRA初始化随机性。\n    fail_f1 mean 75.3%在[72,82]范围下部但≥75%，验证CLS在repo-level的稳定性。 关键洞察：repo-level CLS从function-level\n    88.41%下降到85.5%（-2.9pp）， 下降幅度远小于CWM（从87.4%崩溃到<55%）——这是complexity-dependent advantage的核心证据。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Repo-Level CLS 8B Multi-Seed Results\n    columns:\n    - Seed\n    - Checkpoint\n    - Accuracy\n    - Fail F1\n    - Pass F1\n    - F1 Macro\n    rows:\n    - - 42\n      - ckpt-400\n      - 84.79%\n      - 72.93%\n      - 89.43%\n      - 81.18%\n    - - 123\n      - ckpt-500\n      - 85.8%\n      - 76.2%\n      - 90.1%\n      - 83.2%\n    - - 456\n      - ckpt-450\n      - 85.9%\n      - 76.8%\n      - 90.5%\n      - 83.7%\n    - - Mean±Std\n      - —\n      - 85.5±0.61\n      - 75.3±2.1\n      - 90.0±0.5\n      - 82.7±1.3\n  - name: Function-Level → Repo-Level Drop (CLS vs CWM)\n    columns:\n    - Level\n    - CLS Accuracy (3-seed)\n    - CWM Accuracy\n    - Gap (pp)\n    rows:\n    - - Function (4B)\n      - 88.41%\n      - 87.4%\n      - '+1.0'\n    - - Function (8B)\n      - 89.75%\n      - 87.3%\n      - '+2.43'\n    - - Repo (8B)\n      - 85.5%\n      - <55%*\n      - '>30'\n    footnotes:\n    - '*CWM repo accuracy estimated from parseable predictions only; overall accuracy\n      <55% due to ≥85% unparseable rate'\n  figures_description:\n  - 3-seed accuracy + fail_f1 box plot with CI，展示跨seed稳定性\n  - Function-to-Repo drop comparison bar chart：CLS -2.9pp vs CWM -32+pp\n  analysis: 'Multi-seed验证是best tier的核心数据基础。3-seed std=0.61pp证明repo-level CLS结果不是单次实验的偶然。\n    与function-level的std=0.96pp相比，repo-level variance更小， 可能因为repo-level数据集更大（9784 vs\n    1890 samples），averaging效应更强。 fail_f1的std=2.1pp较大，反映checkpoint selection对precision-recall\n    tradeoff敏感—— 但mean 75.3%稳定≥75%，证明CLS可以在repo-level可靠地检测failing tests。\n\n    '\n- name: Repo-Level CWM Unparseable Rate Confirmation\n  plan_id: repo-level-training\n  description: '确认CWM在repo-level的unparseable rate≥80%是formulation固有缺陷。 整合现有cwm-v10(93%),\n    v11(75.2%), v12(53.7%), cwm-seed123-conda(67.2%)的数据。 用标准化generation config（max_new_tokens=512,\n    匹配典型test output长度）重新评估。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    cwm_8b_unparseable_rate: 0.85\n    cwm_8b_accuracy_overall: 0.52\n    cwm_8b_accuracy_parseable_only: 0.64\n    cwm_8b_fail_f1: 0.18\n    cwm_8b_pass_f1: 0.67\n    cwm_8b_f1_macro: 0.42\n    cwm_8b_truncated_pct: 0.38\n    cwm_8b_string_mismatch_pct: 0.22\n    cwm_8b_clean_correct_pct: 0.1\n    cwm_4b_unparseable_rate: 0.88\n    cwm_4b_accuracy_overall: 0.48\n    majority_baseline: 0.7296\n    cwm_vs_majority_gap_pp: -21.0\n    generation_length_mean_tokens: 487\n    generation_length_median_tokens: 512\n  result_rationale: '现有数据已强烈支持unparseable≥80%：cwm-v10在max_new_tokens=64时93%， cwm-v11在1024时75.2%（但该实验用了subset500且可能有config差异）。\n    标准化config（max_new_tokens=512）下预期85%，原因： (1) Repo-level test execution output通常包含完整stack\n    trace（200-2000 tokens）、 文件路径、版本号、格式化数据结构——CWM需要精确复现这些才能推导pass/fail， 但4B/8B模型无法忠实生成如此复杂的结构化文本；\n    (2) 即使生成了看似合理的output，string-level exact match极低（v10: exact_match约10%）， 因为一个字符的差异（路径分隔符、空格、换行）就导致mismatch；\n    (3) Token budget exhaustion在512 tokens时仍影响38%的predictions—— 许多test output超过512\n    tokens，truncation导致判断信息丢失。 关键论点：CWM的85% unparseable不是调参不足（已尝试10+版本，不同rank/alpha/generation\n    length）， 而是generation formulation在repo-level complexity下的结构性失败—— 要求模型精确生成数百token的结构化文本是一个远难于binary\n    classification的任务。 Overall accuracy 52%低于majority baseline（72.96%），证明CWM在repo-level不仅无优势，\n    实际上worse than trivial baseline。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Repo-Level CWM Failure Mode Breakdown\n    columns:\n    - Category\n    - '% of Predictions'\n    - Description\n    rows:\n    - - Unparseable (total)\n      - 85%\n      - Cannot extract pass/fail from generation\n    - - — Token exhaustion\n      - 38%\n      - Output truncated at max_new_tokens\n    - - — Format failure\n      - 28%\n      - Output structurally invalid\n    - - — String mismatch\n      - 19%\n      - Parseable but wrong surface form\n    - - Parseable & correct\n      - 10%\n      - CWM produces correct output\n    - - Parseable & wrong\n      - 5%\n      - Clean but incorrect prediction\n  - name: CWM Evolution Across Versions\n    columns:\n    - Version\n    - max_new_tokens\n    - Unparseable%\n    - Accuracy%\n    rows:\n    - - v10\n      - 64\n      - 93%\n      - 69.9%*\n    - - v11\n      - 1024\n      - 75.2%\n      - 66.6%\n    - - v12\n      - 512\n      - 53.7%**\n      - 58.0%\n    - - seed123-conda\n      - 512\n      - 67.2%\n      - 59.1%\n    - - Best-tier (standardized)\n      - 512\n      - 85%\n      - 52%\n    footnotes:\n    - '*v10 accuracy inflated: unparseable treated as majority-class prediction'\n    - '**v12 used different training config (longer training, lower LR)'\n  figures_description:\n  - Unparseable rate vs max_new_tokens curve，展示generation length与parsability的tradeoff\n  - CWM failure mode stacked bar：token exhaustion + format failure + string mismatch\n    = 85% total\n  analysis: 'CWM的repo-level失败是formulation-level的必然结果，不是工程问题。 10+版本的迭代（v1到v12，不同seed，不同LoRA配置）consistently产生50-93%\n    unparseable rate， 说明问题出在task formulation而非model/training细节。 这为Claim 1提供了最强的对比：CLS在相同数据上85.5%\n    accuracy vs CWM 52%—— gap超过30pp，远超function-level的0-2.43pp。 Complexity-dependent\n    advantage的narrative完整成立。\n\n    '\n- name: DeepSeek Function-Level Classification\n  plan_id: deepseek-cls-func\n  description: 'DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B-Instruct LoRA fine-tune做function-level per-test\n    binary classification。 与Qwen3-4B CLS对比，验证CLS formulation advantage不是Qwen-specific。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    accuracy: 86.3\n    pass_f1: 86.0\n    fail_f1: 86.5\n    f1_macro: 86.3\n    pass_precision: 90.8\n    pass_recall: 81.5\n    fail_precision: 82.2\n    fail_recall: 91.2\n    train_loss: 0.265\n    eval_loss: 0.078\n    unparseable: 0\n    test_set_size: 1890\n  result_rationale: 'DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B（2023年12月）比Qwen3-4B（2025年5月）多~1.7x参数， 但属于旧generation，code\n    understanding能力与Qwen3-4B大致equivalent。 预期accuracy 86.3%略低于Qwen3-4B multi-seed mean（88.41%），\n    因为DeepSeek的pretraining data cutoff更早，对newer coding patterns覆盖不足。 但86.3%仍然远高于majority\n    baseline（51.75%）和zero-shot LLM-judge（64.4%）， 证明fine-tuned classification在不同架构上consistently有效。\n    关键发现：DeepSeek CLS accuracy（86.3%）与DeepSeek CWM accuracy（85.7%）的gap仅0.6pp—— 这复现了Qwen3-4B上的null\n    result（gap 1.0pp at 4B）， 确认function-level CLS≈CWM equivalence是architecture-independent的。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'DeepSeek CLS结果是hypothesis 3的关键支撑。 如果gap仅在Qwen上存在，reviewer可以质疑这是Qwen-specific\n    artifact。 DeepSeek复现消除了这个concern。\n\n    '\n- name: DeepSeek Function-Level CWM + Multi-Seed\n  plan_id: deepseek-cwm-func\n  description: 'DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B LoRA CWM generation baseline + seed123多seed验证。\n    与DeepSeek CLS对比确认function-level null result的architecture independence。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    seed42_cwm_accuracy: 85.7\n    seed42_cwm_pass_f1: 85.4\n    seed42_cwm_fail_f1: 86.0\n    seed42_cwm_exact_match: 80.5\n    seed42_cwm_unparseable: 0\n    seed123_cwm_accuracy: 86.1\n    seed123_cwm_pass_f1: 85.8\n    seed123_cwm_fail_f1: 86.3\n    seed42_cls_accuracy: 86.3\n    cls_cwm_gap_seed42_pp: 0.6\n    cls_cwm_gap_seed123_pp: 0.2\n    cls_cwm_gap_mean_pp: 0.4\n    cls_cwm_gap_95ci_lower: -0.9\n    cls_cwm_gap_95ci_upper: 1.7\n    paired_ttest_pvalue: 0.68\n  result_rationale: 'DeepSeek CWM在function-level预期accuracy 85.7%，与CLS的86.3%差距仅0.6pp。\n    这复现了Qwen3-4B上的pattern：CWM 87.4% vs CLS 88.41%（gap ~1.0pp）。 DeepSeek的exact match\n    rate（80.5%）低于Qwen3-4B（84.02%）， 因为DeepSeek对function-level output format的生成精度略低——\n    但由于function-level output短（<50 tokens），这些format差异不影响pass/fail判断。 seed123 CWM（86.1%）与seed42（85.7%）的差异（0.4pp）在正常随机性范围内。\n    两seed的CLS-CWM gap（0.6pp和0.2pp）mean=0.4pp，95% CI [-0.9, 1.7]包含0， p=0.68远超0.05，cleanly确认function-level\n    null result。 关键指标：deepseek_func_cls_cwm_gap_pp = 0.4pp，在best tier范围[-1.0, 1.5]内。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: DeepSeek vs Qwen Function-Level Comparison\n    columns:\n    - Architecture\n    - Size\n    - CLS Acc\n    - CWM Acc\n    - Gap (pp)\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3\n      - 4B\n      - 88.41%\n      - 87.4%\n      - '+1.0'\n    - - Qwen3\n      - 8B\n      - 89.75%\n      - 87.3%\n      - '+2.43'\n    - - DeepSeek-Coder\n      - 6.7B\n      - 86.3%\n      - 85.7%\n      - '+0.6'\n  - name: DeepSeek Multi-Seed CWM\n    columns:\n    - Seed\n    - CWM Acc\n    - CLS Acc\n    - Gap (pp)\n    rows:\n    - - 42\n      - 85.7%\n      - 86.3%\n      - '+0.6'\n    - - 123\n      - 86.1%\n      - 86.3%*\n      - '+0.2'\n    - - Mean\n      - 85.9%\n      - 86.3%\n      - '+0.4'\n    footnotes:\n    - '*CLS只训练了seed42，此处复用同一CLS模型'\n  figures_description:\n  - Architecture-independent null result visualization：Qwen3-4B, Qwen3-8B, DeepSeek-6.7B三组bar\n    pairs，function-level gap均在噪声范围内\n  - DeepSeek CLS vs CWM per-class F1 comparison，CI完全重叠\n  analysis: 'DeepSeek复现是best tier叙事的关键一环。三个architecture×size配置的function-level gap：\n    Qwen3-4B: +1.0pp, Qwen3-8B: +2.43pp, DeepSeek-6.7B: +0.6pp。 function-level gap始终在0-2.5pp范围内，与repo-level\n    >30pp形成鲜明对比。 这排除了\"CLS advantage是Qwen architecture artifact\"的reviewer concern。\n    注意Qwen3-8B的2.43pp gap已经开始diverge——这preview了repo-level的趋势， 更大模型+更复杂任务下CWM failure\n    modes逐渐显现。 DeepSeek作为完全不同的architecture（不同tokenizer、不同attention实现、不同pretraining\n    data） 仍然reproduce null result，说明这是task-level property而非model-level artifact。\n\n    '\n- name: DeepSeek Repo-Level Classification\n  plan_id: deepseek-cls-repo\n  description: 'DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B LoRA classification在repo-level SWE-bench-PerTest数据上。\n    验证classification formulation的repo-level advantage在不同architecture下是否保持。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    accuracy: 81.5\n    f1_macro: 76.8\n    fail_f1: 65.2\n    pass_f1: 88.4\n    fail_precision: 68.5\n    fail_recall: 62.1\n    pass_precision: 85.3\n    pass_recall: 91.7\n    unparseable: 0\n    majority_baseline: 72.96\n    gap_vs_majority_pp: 8.5\n    qwen8b_repo_accuracy: 85.5\n    deepseek_vs_qwen_gap_pp: -4.0\n    deepseek_func_to_repo_drop_pp: -4.8\n  result_rationale: 'DeepSeek repo-level CLS预期81.5% accuracy，低于Qwen3-8B的85.5%（-4.0pp），原因：\n    (1) DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B的context window限制（16K vs Qwen3-8B的32K）， repo-level input平均6.8K\n    tokens，更多cases需要truncation； (2) DeepSeek的code understanding在repo-level cross-file\n    dependencies上弱于newer Qwen3， pretraining data中repo-level code comprehension的覆盖不足；\n    (3) 6.7B vs 8B的参数差距虽小，但Qwen3架构效率更高（GQA + sliding window attention）。 从function-level\n    86.3%到repo-level 81.5%的drop（-4.8pp）与Qwen3-8B的drop（-4.3pp）相近， 说明classification\n    formulation在不同architecture上有consistent的degradation pattern。 关键发现：DeepSeek repo-level\n    CLS（81.5%）仍然远高于majority baseline（72.96%）， 证明classification formulation即使在非SOTA\n    architecture上也能provide reliable verification。 如果DeepSeek CWM repo-level也像Qwen\n    CWM一样unparseable≥80%， 则完全确认advantage是formulation-driven而非architecture-driven。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cross-Architecture Repo-Level CLS Comparison\n    columns:\n    - Architecture\n    - Size\n    - Func CLS Acc\n    - Repo CLS Acc\n    - Drop (pp)\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3\n      - 4B\n      - 88.41%\n      - ~83.6%*\n      - -4.8\n    - - Qwen3\n      - 8B\n      - 89.75%\n      - 85.5%\n      - -4.3\n    - - DeepSeek-Coder\n      - 6.7B\n      - 86.3%\n      - 81.5%\n      - -4.8\n    footnotes:\n    - '*4B repo results from cls4b-v5-ckpt4600 test eval'\n  figures_description:\n  - Function → Repo accuracy drop comparison across architectures，三组paired bars展示consistent\n    ~4-5pp drop\n  analysis: 'DeepSeek repo-level CLS是supplementary evidence，不是核心result。 其价值在于展示classification\n    formulation的robustness across architectures： 即使换一个完全不同的model family，repo-level\n    CLS仍然work（>>majority baseline）， 而CWM仍然fail（unparseable dominant）。 这是architecture\n    independence claim在repo-level的延伸验证。\n\n    '\n- name: Repo-Level Error Complementarity & Oracle Ensemble\n  plan_id: repo-level-training\n  description: '分析repo-level CLS和CWM（parseable subset）的error complementarity。 计算oracle\n    ensemble accuracy——如果两个模型的错误不重叠，ensemble ceiling多高。 扩展function-level的complementarity\n    finding（oracle=90.63%）到repo-level。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    cls_repo_accuracy: 85.5\n    cwm_repo_accuracy_parseable: 64.0\n    cwm_repo_parseable_pct: 15.0\n    oracle_accuracy_parseable_subset: 91.2\n    cls_error_type_dominant: miss_bug (false_negative)\n    cwm_error_type_dominant: false_alarm + unparseable\n    complementarity_rate: 0.68\n    cls_only_correct_pct: 34.5\n    cwm_only_correct_pct: 8.2\n    both_correct_pct: 48.8\n    both_wrong_pct: 8.5\n    n_parseable_samples: 1468\n  result_rationale: 'Repo-level complementarity analysis限于CWM parseable subset（~15%\n    of total，~1468 samples）。 在这个subset上，CLS accuracy ~85.5%，CWM accuracy ~64%—— 但两者的error\n    pattern高度complementary（complementarity rate 0.68）。 CLS的dominant error是miss bugs（false\n    negative）：模型对长context中的subtle bugs不敏感， 倾向于predict pass。CWM的dominant error是false\n    alarms： 生成的output与gold不完全match被判为fail，即使语义上patch是correct的。 Oracle ensemble在parseable\n    subset上达91.2%，证明两种formulation捕获不同的code semantics。 但CWM的85% unparseable严重限制了ensemble的实际应用——\n    只有15%的predictions可以ensemble，对overall accuracy的提升有限。 这为paper提供了nuanced finding：complementarity存在但CWM的formulation\n    bottleneck 使其无法被充分利用。Future work可以探索更好的generation formulation来保留complementarity\n    同时降低unparseable rate。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Repo-Level Error Complementarity (Parseable Subset)\n    columns:\n    - Category\n    - '%'\n    rows:\n    - - Both correct\n      - 48.8%\n    - - CLS only correct\n      - 34.5%\n    - - CWM only correct\n      - 8.2%\n    - - Both wrong\n      - 8.5%\n    - - Oracle accuracy\n      - 91.2%\n  - name: Function vs Repo Error Complementarity\n    columns:\n    - Level\n    - CLS Acc\n    - CWM Acc\n    - Oracle Acc\n    - Complementarity\n    rows:\n    - - Function (4B)\n      - 87.5%\n      - 87.5%\n      - 90.63%\n      - 0.72\n    - - Repo (8B, parseable)\n      - 85.5%\n      - 64.0%\n      - 91.2%\n      - 0.68\n  figures_description:\n  - Venn diagram of error overlap at repo-level，展示CLS和CWM的error union structure\n  analysis: 'Repo-level complementarity结果有两面性： (1) 好消息：在parseable subset上oracle达91.2%，与function-level的90.63%相近，\n    说明CLS和CWM在能work的cases上仍然是complementary的。 (2) 坏消息：85% unparseable意味着ensemble只覆盖15%的predictions。\n    论文中应frame为：complementarity是formulation-level property（与complexity无关）， 但CWM的generation\n    bottleneck在高complexity下限制了其utility。 这motivates future work on improved generation\n    formulations that maintain complementarity while achieving better parsability。\n\n    '\n- name: Diagnostic Re-repair Experiment\n  plan_id: diagnostic-rerepair\n  description: '200-instance downstream proof-of-concept：repair agent在per-test failure\n    predictions 指导下vs无per-test信息，比较resolve rate。使用SWE-agent framework。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_instances: 200\n    baseline_resolve_rate_pct: 27.0\n    rerepair_blind_resolve_rate_pct: 29.5\n    rerepair_with_diagnostics_resolve_rate_pct: 33.0\n    diagnostic_lift_pp: 6.0\n    blind_lift_pp: 2.5\n    diagnostic_specific_lift_pp: 3.5\n    n_initially_unresolved: 146\n    n_rerepair_triggered: 92\n    rerepair_success_with_diag_pct: 25.0\n    rerepair_success_without_diag_pct: 13.0\n    mcnemar_pvalue: 0.022\n    multi_f2p_diagnostic_lift_pp: 11.5\n    single_f2p_diagnostic_lift_pp: 2.0\n    multi_f2p_n_instances: 62\n    single_f2p_n_instances: 138\n    avg_rerepair_attempts: 1.8\n    per_test_prediction_accuracy_on_tested: 84.2\n  result_rationale: 'Diagnostic lift 6.0pp（best tier范围[3,8]）的机制： (1) Per-test predictions为repair\n    agent提供failure localization—— 当agent知道\"test_parse_edge_case fails but test_basic\n    passes\"时， 修复集中在edge case logic而非盲目重试entire solution； (2) Blind re-repair（知道unresolved但不知哪个test\n    fail）仍有2.5pp lift， 因为SWE-agent的retry本身就有correction概率—— 但diagnostic-specific增量3.5pp证明per-test信息的独特贡献；\n    (3) 优势严重集中于multi-F2P instances： T≥2时lift 11.5pp vs T=1时仅2.0pp，与oracle analysis预测完全一致。\n    原因：T=1时per-test info等价于trajectory info（只有一个fail test， 知道\"有test fail\"和知道\"test_X\n    fail\"信息量相同）； T≥2时per-test info区分了不同failure patterns， repair agent可以逐个target failing\n    tests而非guess which test fails。 McNemar p=0.022在200样本下达到显著性（<0.05）—— 虽然样本量有限但足以支撑proof-of-concept级别的claim。\n    92/146 re-repair triggered表明63%的unresolved instances至少尝试了re-repair； with diagnostics的25%\n    success rate vs without的13%证明信息质量差异。 Per-test prediction accuracy on re-repair测试的84.2%与overall\n    85.5%接近， 说明re-repair并未选择性地作用于easy/hard cases。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Diagnostic Re-repair Results\n    columns:\n    - Condition\n    - Resolve Rate\n    - Δ vs Baseline\n    rows:\n    - - No re-repair (baseline)\n      - 27.0%\n      - —\n    - - Re-repair without diagnostics\n      - 29.5%\n      - +2.5 pp\n    - - Re-repair with per-test diagnostics\n      - 33.0%\n      - +6.0 pp\n    - - Diagnostic-specific lift\n      - —\n      - +3.5 pp (p=0.022)\n  - name: Diagnostic Lift Stratified by F2P Count\n    columns:\n    - F2P Count\n    - N Instances\n    - Diag Lift\n    - Blind Lift\n    rows:\n    - - T=1\n      - 138\n      - +2.0 pp\n      - +1.5 pp\n    - - T≥2\n      - 62\n      - +11.5 pp\n      - +3.8 pp\n    - - Overall\n      - 200\n      - +6.0 pp\n      - +2.5 pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: three conditions × T=1 vs T≥2 stratification'\n  - 'Per-instance resolve rate improvement scatter: x=N failing tests, y=resolve rate\n    delta'\n  analysis: Re-repair实验完成了Claim 2的实证闭环：per-test classification不仅在accuracy上等价于trajectory\n    （TOST p=0.007），还提供了actionable的diagnostic信息带来6pp resolve rate improvement。 Stratification连接Claim\n    2和Claim 3：advantage集中在multi-F2P instances（与oracle预测一致）， 为部署决策提供了清晰框架——在multi-F2P场景下per-test\n    verification的ROI最高。 论文应定位为proof-of-concept，目标是展示mechanism而非claim SOTA repair performance。\n    200 instances是moderate sample size，sufficient for significance但reviewer可能要求larger\n    scale—— frame为future work方向。\n","numLines":622,"startLine":1,"totalLines":622}}}
